          "final_text_tail": "\n\nBoth tasks are complete. All changes are in `llama-index-core/llama_index/core/base/llms/types.py`:\n\n**Task 1 \u2014 Lazy MIME type accessor** (types.py:89):\n- New `get_image_mimetype()` method: returns `image_mimetype` if already set; otherwise guesses via `filetype.guess` on the raw image bytes and caches the result for future accesses.\n- `image_to_base64` no longer contains inline guessing logic \u2014 it delegates to `get_image_mimetype()`.\n\n**Task 2 \u2014 `encoding` field** (types.py:58):\n- New `encoding: Literal[\"base64\", \"raw\"] = \"base64\"` field; default preserves existing behavior.\n- `image_to_base64` now branches on the field, skipping base64 encoding when `encoding=\"raw\"`.\n- `resolve_image` was updated to match the storage mode (raw bytes returned as-is / encoded on demand), so raw blocks work end-to-end.\n\nVerification:\n- All 12 existing tests in `tests/base/llms/test_types.py` pass.\n- Sanity checks confirmed: default base64 encoding, raw byte preservation, `encoding` value validation (invalid values rejected), lazy mimetype resolution + caching, pre-set mimetype not re-guessed, unguessable data \u2192 `None`, path/URL not loaded for guessing, and `ChatMessage` serialization roundtrip with the new field.\n- The single failing test in `tests/llms` (`test_llm_astream_chat_handles_nonyielding_stream`) fails identically on the original code \u2014 pre-existing and unrelated.",
